Donors
------
- Komikku (Komikku app) — PRIMARY donor.
  https://github.com/komikku-app/Komikku @ 1656575e8fdaaef010c652f9758130c2a01d8890
  Modules used: source-api (eu.kanade.tachiyomi.source.*) and core/common
  (eu.kanade.tachiyomi.network.*, tachiyomi.core.common.*, mihon.core.common.*).
- Mihon (mihonapp/mihon) — upstream of Komikku; fallback donor. Used for the
  plain `network` lookup shape in HttpSource (Komikku's copy is entangled with
  its TachiyomiSY delegated-source machinery, see Deviations).
- Keiyoushi extensions-lib — the binary contract, not a code donor.
  https://github.com/keiyoushi/extensions-lib @ 42255ee5fa96d9425697b7c143587483207308d1
  Real Keiyoushi extensions were compiled against these stubs; every class and
  member in that stub set is present here with a matching JVM signature
  (verified mechanically at transplant time — see KEIYOUSHI-PLAYER-PLAN §K1).

What was copied verbatim
------------------------
 Komikku source-api: SourceFactory, UnmeteredSource, ConfigurableSource,
   SManga, SChapter, SMangaImpl, SChapterImpl, Page, SMangaUpdate,
   UpdateStrategy.
 Komikku core/common: HttpException, AndroidCookieJar, NetworkPreferences
   (minus a block the donor itself keeps commented out), ProgressListener,
   ProgressResponseBody, DohProviders, Requests, the four interceptors
   (UncaughtException, UserAgent, RateLimit, SpecificHostRateLimit),
   JsonObject.EMPTY (mihon.core.common.extensions), the preference framework
   (Preference, PreferenceStore, AndroidPreference, AndroidPreferenceStore),
   and LogcatExtensions (see deviation 12).
 Keiyoushi extensions-lib (contract text): CatalogueSource, FilterList.

Deviations and substitutions (complete list)
--------------------------------------------
1. Source / HttpSource — the deprecated RxJava fetch* bridges and Komikku's
   Source-level related-manga/query-sanitiser machinery are dropped (RxJava
   and the lib-1.4 surface are out of scope per the K1 plan; "Lib 1.6 only").
   Source.getFilterList carries Komikku's production default body
   (FilterList()) instead of the stub's compile-time throw, because extensions
   that don't override it dispatch to the host's default implementation.
   HttpSource keeps Komikku's related-manga block (it is self-contained).
2. HttpSource.network — upstream (Mihon) shape: `Injekt.get<NetworkHelper>()`.
   Komikku wraps it in an anonymous NetworkHelper subclass serving its
   TachiyomiSY/EH delegated sources (exh.* app internals); that wrapper and
   the EXH delegate block (delegate/bindDelegate) are not carried, and
   HttpSource.client reads network.client directly.
3. HttpSource.getImageUrl — body composes imageUrlRequest/imageUrlParse via
   awaitSuccess(); the direct suspend equivalent of Komikku's
   fetchImageUrl(page).awaitSingle() RxJava bridge.
4. NetworkHelper — Komikku's CloudflareInterceptor is NOT wired into the
   client builders in this slice: Komikku's interceptor raises Komikku's own
   WebView UI and strings. Slice K2 inserts Xreader's adapted interceptor,
   which routes challenges through Xreader's sanctioned solve-or-sign-in
   screen and bridges cookies to Xreader's session store. Komikku's
   EHLogLevel-gated HTTP logging block is dropped (exh.* app internal).
   A secondary (Context) constructor is added, restoring the extension-lib
   (Context) shape on top of Komikku's primary (Context, NetworkPreferences)
   constructor, backed by the donor AndroidPreferenceStore.
5. AppInfo — Komikku's getters read its app module's BuildConfig, which a
   library module cannot see. The two contract getters return values held in
   internal vars (default 0 / "") that the Xreader app sets at startup (K2).
   Komikku's getSupportedImageMimeTypes() is not in the extension-lib 1.6
   contract (it needs Komikku's ImageUtil) and is not carried.
6. JavaScriptEngine — WIRED in K6 (was a deliberate named stub in K1).
   The real implementation is Komikku's (Apache-2.0), QuickJS-backed,
   transplanted verbatim except one named substitution: the donor's
   withIOContext becomes withContext(Dispatchers.IO). The K6 survey
   DEX-scanned the whole live Keiyoushi index (1,449 extensions,
   2026-11-01): ZERO reference this class as a type descriptor or as a
   dotted string, and an OkHttp sanity needle hit 1,449/1,449, so the
   zero is a true negative for today's repo. The engine is wired anyway
   because the transplant is contained (this class + api(libs.quickjs
   .android) here + one Injekt singleton registration in the player's
   registrar) and the index is live: a JS-using source can appear in any
   repo update and works the day it lands, instead of failing with the
   stub's named refusal.
7. Filter — Komikku's fork-only Filter.AutoComplete subclass (TachiyomiSY) is
   not carried; it is outside the lib-1.6 contract and would grow the sealed
   hierarchy extensions were compiled against. FilterList follows the
   contract's plain data class (Komikku's copy adds a Compose @Stable
   annotation and an always-false equals() for its own UI).
8. MangasPage — final class with plain vals, per the contract. Komikku makes
   it open solely for its exh MetadataMangasPage subclass (Komikku metadata
   framework), which is not carried; the contract's component1/component2/
   copy members are Komikku's own and are kept.
9. OkHttpExtensions — the RxJava asObservable/asObservableSuccess bridges and
   the parseAs/decodeFromJsonResponse helpers are not carried (RxJava surface;
   parseAs additionally needs Kotlin context receivers and the
   kotlinx-serialization json-okio artifact, and is outside the contract).
   await, awaitSuccess, newCachelessCallWithProgress and jsonMime are
   Komikku's, verbatim.
10. PreferenceScreen — Komikku declares expect/actual across its multiplatform
    source sets; in this plain Android library the same typealias stands
    without the actual keyword. It erases identically in signatures.
11. OkHttp version seam — the donors build against OkHttp 5, where
    Response.body is non-null; Xreader's catalog pins OkHttp 4.12.0, where it
    is nullable. Two donor call sites carry a `!!` (NetworkHelper's
    saveResponseToFile, OkHttpExtensions' newCachelessCallWithProgress),
    marked in code. Nothing else in the transplant touches an OkHttp-5-only
    API. (The K2 spike decides whether the player forces an OkHttp upgrade.)
12. LogcatExtensions — the `logcat.logcat` import is aliased (logcatImpl) so
    the delegate call inside Any.logcat() is unambiguous under Xreader's
    Kotlin 2.0.21 (the donor compiles against a newer Kotlin). Behaviour is
    unchanged.
13. NetworkHelper and Page are `open` (Komikku's shape) where the stub
    classes are final. Verified safe at transplant time: every member
    signature matches the contract exactly, and no extension compiled against
    the stub can subclass a class its stub declared final, so the difference
    is unobservable to extension code. (Komikku's host needs both open.)
14. AppInfo (K2) — a public setVersionInfo(versionCode, versionName) host
    hook is added. Komikku's getters read its own app-module BuildConfig;
    this module cannot see the host app's BuildConfig, so Xreader's app sets
    the two internal values through the hook once at startup (AppContainer).
    Extension-facing behaviour is unchanged: the getters report the host
    app's real version code/name.
15. NetworkHelper.cookieJar (K2) — the declared type is widened from the
    donor's AndroidCookieJar to okhttp3.CookieJar. Komikku never substitutes
    the jar; Xreader's player must (its SessionStore-backed jar resolves
    cookies per-source-host from the encrypted session store, per the D2
    rule — never the global WebView jar). The default instance remains the
    verbatim AndroidCookieJar, and nothing in the extension contract
    references the narrower type.

Fork merge markers (SY/KMK/EXH) present in the donor files were stripped
during the transplant; they carry no semantics outside the donor repo.
